    "turn_text": "and here's the thing eric the folks that went to martha's vineyard you know by then it's having people go to the federal government is basically as i know they do fly some people around but mostly people just abandoned so these people were basically home what i mean they had no where where really to integrate to And so this was a huge benefit for them. They've actually, some of those folks have written into the vendor, thanking the vendor for being able to effectuate their transport. So they went, clearly it was beneficial for them to be able to do it. Now obviously Martha's Vineyard didn't want anything to do with it, and so they deported them. But the reality is, when you hear some of the people acting like it's inhumane to transfer to a sanctuary jurisdiction, That doesn't make any sense because they're in destitution basically because of the federal government's really reckless policies. At the end of the day, Martha's Vineyard didn't want to put their money where their mouth is. I understand that. I think they're willing to virtue signal if it's just self-congratulatory type stuff, but they really didn't want to follow through with it. But it has raised the issue now of this border because the corporate press doesn't want to talk about any of the things that a lot of conservatives have been concerned with a long time. defense and also affected florida we've had criminal aliens commit serious crimes uh... against floridians and then we do have just kind of the migrants who a lot of them you know they are not necessarily committing crimes they did their economic migrants but that that causes stress on communities as we saw even the wealth one of the wealthiest in the country said they didn't have the resources that they care of fifty out of these border towns do so all those are important but also just think as an american people look at the okay Do you have control over your border and your territory or not? And it makes us look like a third world country when you see all these images coming in of just chaos day after day after day. Well now people are talking about it and I think people are going to have to defend who are who are who are providing policy. They're going to have to defend it and you know it's pretty much indefensible.",
