    "turn_text": "You know, we were down there a couple weeks ago. My daughter wants to be a rocket engineer. She wanted to go to NASA for her birthday. The thing that really struck me, I mean, I go to Florida all the time. It was the first time I noticed it is the rest stops along the way. They're the counters. So the 18 wheelers know how many spaces are available. They can pull in and not have to park on the side of the road like they do in so many states. I was actually really impressed with that project that's been implemented in the state over the years. I'd never seen anything like it. And sure was handy that we weren't having to dodge 18 wheelers trying to pull off the side of the road to meet their hours at night. They had a place to pull in. Speaking of infrastructure down there, you've got this explosive growth, and I'm always struck by progressive friends of mine who some of them don't even particularly care for you, but they always remark that you've done a really good job as governor balancing the explosion of growth, but also the environmental concerns and the diverse ecology in Florida. How do you, as a Republican, when Democrats go all in on climate change stuff, how do you look at it as public policy to balance the environment and the economy?",
